      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-03-09_WidnesExaminer_art0142" n="art0142">
        <head>Workingmen's Mission, Bank Quay.</head>
        <p>Workingmen's Mission, Bank Quay.</p>
        <p>- Another of the series of concerts, arranged by the workers in connection with the forthcoming bazaar, was held on Thursday night, in the Schoolroom, the proceeds on this occasion being on behalf of the Congregational and Society Class Stall. An excellent programme was submitted the following being the artiste' s songs by Miss L Duckworth. Mrs Townroe, and Mr Poole. Recitations by Mr Wright, humorous recital by Mr Townroe, humorous songs by Mr. Howie. sketches by the Bewsey Adult School Party, and Mrs. J. Hassell and party. Captain Crostield presided over a good attendance. During the evening light refresh- ments were provided. On the motion of Mr. G. Dale a very hearty vote of thanks was accorded to the chair. man and artistes for their services.</p>
