        <p>COUNTY • BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. WANTED, an OFFICE BOY, between the ages' of 131 and 15 years, for the ELECTRICITY DEPART- I MENT. Wages 88. per week, rising to a maximum of los. One with knowledge of shorthand, Typewriting and General Office Work preferred. Applications (on form to be obtained from F. V. L. Mathias, Borough Electrical and Tramways Engineer, Electricity Works, Howley), to be returned not later than Saturday, March 16th, 1912. Applicants, whose parents must be ratepayers of Warrington, will be required to sit for a Competitive Examination. J. r...YoN WHITTLE, Town Hall, Bth March, 1912. Town Clerk. GREAT WESTERN RAILWAY.—The Great Western Railway Company HEREBY GIVE NOTICE that owing to the COLLIERS' STRIKE it may become necessary to curtail or even discontinue certain Goods Train Services, and Merchandise Traffic of every description can only be accepted for conveyance at the risk of the sender. The Company further give notice that they cannot accept responsibility for loss, damage, or delay of any kind in connection with the conveyance or delivery of such merchandise traffics as is accepted, but will endeavour to afford the best service practicable in the circumstances. (Signed) FRANK POTTER, March, 1912. General Manager. CHESHIRE COUNTY COUNCIL. TO CARTERS, FARMERS, AND TEAM OWNERS. 11)1 ERSONS desirous of TENDERING for CARTING MACADAM and other Materials for the Main Boads for the year ending 31st March, 1913, can obtain Forms of Tender, and particulars of material to be carted, at the County Surveyor's Office, Chester Castle, on and after Monday, the 4th March, 1912, between 9 a.m. and 5.30 p.m., and on Saturdays between 9 a.m. and 1 p.m. Tenders, endorsed "Tender for Carting," to be delivered at the said office on or before Saturday the 16th March next. The Main Roads Committee of the County Council do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any Tender. HARRY F. BULL. County Surveyor. 29th February, 1912.</p>
