        <p>EXHIBITIONS, ETC. WAKE UP, ENGLAND ! ! A GREAT INTERNATIONAL and UNIVERSAL EXHIBITION is to be held in GHENT in 1013 in which Great Britain cannot afford not to be represented officially. Belgium is our best Continental Customer, comparatively with the size of the Country. Ghent is admirably situated on the main road from the Continent to England. Every nation alike will be ready to come to the neutral ground of Belgium for this great exhibition. Already the German Committee, ever alert to seize the passing opportunity, encouraged by their sale at Brussels, 1910, has signed an agreement to con- struct a special pavilion, which will be one of the most striking points of the Exhibition. The Congress of the United States of America that refused to contribute to the Brussels Exhibition has, at the request of President Taft, consented to exhibit officially at Ghent. The Government of Greene the same. France,with characteristic enterprise, is taking twice as much space as she had in Brussels, and is asking for more. Italy will have a fine Official Exhibit. The Canadian Government bas secured a prominent position for an Official Exhibit. Negotiations are on the point of termination with Russia. The far- off countries of Coins and Japan, Chili, Peru, Brazil, and Cuba, the Argentine Republic, New Zealand and India will all be there. EXHIBIT OR LOSE THE TRADE. Apply for Plan, Booklets and Information, gratis and post free. CHARLES KNOTT, ROOM 5, GHENT EXHIBITION OFFICES 1, SOUTHAMPTON ROW, LONDON, W.C.</p>
