        <p>GOLF. WARRINGTON. CAPTAIN'S MEDAL COMPETITION. The twelfth round of this competition was played on Saturday. The scores were : FIRST DIVISION. Gross. H'cap. Net. F Pendlebury BB 7 81 J M Murray C II Ilusworth E A Connor 93 5 88 SECOND DIVISION. B S Newcpmbe lO3 17 86 0 Lofthouse R T Fairclough J H Clarke A Warbuf ton • A GOLDEN WEDDING. Mr. and Mrs. Thomas Lord, Haydock-street, Earles- town, celebrated their golden wedding on Saturday. They were married in the parish of Lowton, two or three miles away, in March, 1662. Mr. Lord is seventy- five years of age, and his wife is in her seventy-second year. They have bad fourteen children, seven of whom are alive. -</p>
